ive cutpoint (>0.25) specification gave risk diff 0.219pp, OR 1.189, p=0.002", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["alternative cutpoint specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[162, 162]], "assertion": "adding league country as a covariate gave risk diff 0.185pp, OR 1.167, p=0.004", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league country specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 140, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "adding league and position covariates gave a risk difference of approximately 0.180 percentage points (row is garbled/truncated in source, remaining values unreadable)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league+position specification"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 141, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[164, 164]], "assertion": "no correction for multiple testing was applied; one- and two-sided p-values are reported unadjusted", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiplicity correction"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 142, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[165, 165]], "assertion": "reported effect sizes and significance are optimized for this specific dataset and should be read as upper bounds on the strength of evidence", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size estimates"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 143, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[166, 166]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 144, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[167, 167]], "assertion": "the results are proof-of-concept evidence and should not be treated as definitive causal estimates", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["causal interpretation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [145]}, {"id": 145, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[167, 167]], "assertion": "a preregistered replication with independent data and a priori specifications is recommended as the appropriate next step, but was not conducted here", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["preregistered replication"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [144]}, {"id": 146, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[168, 168]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[169, 169]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[170, 170]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[171, 171]], "note": "label heading"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[172, 172]], "assertion": "the >0.125 cutpoint, though data-driven, is defended as having face validity by separating the lightest skin tones from all others", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cutpoint defensibility"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[173, 173]], "assertion": "the cutpoint aligns with a natural break in the rater scale structure", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["cutpoint defensibility"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 152, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[174, 174]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses show the effect persists with alternative cutpoints, though with reduced magnitude", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses", "cutpoints"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 153, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[175, 175]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[176, 176]], "note": "label heading"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[177, 177]], "assertion": "power and simplicity were prioritized by adjusting only for exposure (games played)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariate adjustment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 156, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[178, 178]], "assertion": "minimal adjustment was justified on the grounds that overadjustment can introduce collider bias or mask true effects", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariate adjustment rationale"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 157, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[179, 179]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses controlling for league and position show attenuation but sustained significance, suggesting the primary estimate may reflect both direct and indirect pathways", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses", "confounding pathways"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 158, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[181, 181]], "note": "label heading"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[182, 182]], "assertion": "player-referee dyads were used as the analysis level to maximize sample size and power", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["dyad-level analysis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [161]}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[182, 182]], "assertion": "player-level aggregation and individual match-level analysis were not used", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["player-level analysis", "match-level analysis"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [160]}, {"id": 162, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[183, 183]], "assertion": "the dyad-level analysis assumes independence across dyads, an assumption that may be violated by clustering within players and referees", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["independence assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[184, 184]], "assertion": "hierarchical/random-effects models were not used in the primary specification, because they add complexity and can reduce power in rare-event settings", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["hierarchical models", "random effects"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[185, 185]], "assertion": "the independence assumption is favorable to finding an effect, though described as standard in many observational studies", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["independence assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[186, 186]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[187, 187]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[189, 189]], "note": "list label"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "speculative confounding by playing style, no specific action asserted"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "adjusting for position in sensitivity analyses attenuates the effect, suggesting partial confounding", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["position adjustment", "confounding"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 171, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[192, 192]], "note": "residual confounding possible, no specific action"}, {"id": 172, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[193, 193]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 173, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[194, 194]], "note": "list label"}, {"id": 174, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[195, 197]], "note": "caveats about measurement error/misclassification from photo-based ratings and dichotomization, no specific new action"}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[198, 198]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[199, 199]], "note": "list label"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[200, 200]], "assertion": "21,407 dyads (15%) were excluded due to missing skin tone ratings", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing skin tone", "exclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 178, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[201, 202]], "note": "caveat that missingness-related bias is possible but unevidenced"}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[203, 203]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[204, 204]], "note": "list label"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[205, 205]], "assertion": "implicit/explicit referee bias scores exist only aggregated at the country level, not measured for individual referees", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["referee bias measures"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[206, 206]], "assertion": "the country-level bias measures were not used in the primary specification, though available in the data", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee bias measures"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 183, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[207, 207]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 184, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[208, 208]], "note": "list label"}, {"id": 185, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[209, 209]], "note": "cannot rule out reverse causation/unmeasured confounding"}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[210, 210]], "note": "causal interpretation requires strong assumptions"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[211, 211]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[212, 212]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[213, 213]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[214, 214]], "assertion": "several choices were made that are defensible but favor finding a significant effect, in order to maximize in-sample evidence", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["analytic choices"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[215, 215]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[216, 216]], "assertion": "no cross-validation was used; the full sample served for both model development and testing", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["cross-validation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 193, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[217, 217]], "assertion": "two-sided p-values are reported, but the exploratory framework emphasizes the one-sided/directional hypothesis", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["hypothesis framing", "p-values"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 194, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[218, 218]], "assertion": "the dichotomization threshold was chosen to maximize the effect, which inflates Type I error risk", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cutpoint selection", "Type I error"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 195, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[219, 219]], "assertion": "fewer covariates were used for greater power, at higher risk of confounding", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariate adjustment"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 196, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[220, 220]], "assertion": "a standard percentile bootstrap (potentially slightly anticonservative) was used rather than a bias-corrected bootstrap, which would have produced wider CIs", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["bootstrap method"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 197, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[221, 221]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 198, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[222, 222]], "assertion": "these choices are described as transparent and reproducible, with all sensitivity checks remaining supportive, lending credibility to the finding", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["analytic choices", "reproducibility"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 199, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[223, 223]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 200, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[224, 224]], "note": "horizontal rule"}, {"id": 201, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[225, 225]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 202, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[226, 226]], "note": "section heading"}, {"id": 203, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[227, 227]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 204, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[228, 228]], "assertion": "the analysis provides strong in-sample evidence that dark-skin-toned players receive red cards at a higher rate, robust and consistent across specifications", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["main finding"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 205, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[229, 229]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 206, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[230, 230]], "note": "label heading"}, {"id": 207, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[231, 231]], "assertion": "the 0.254pp difference corresponds to roughly a 23% relative increase in red card probability (from 1.10% to 1.37% unadjusted)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["relative increase"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 208, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[232, 232]], "note": "argument about real-world stakes/importance of the finding"}, {"id": 209, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[233, 233]], "note": "reference to broader implicit-bias literature"}, {"id": 210, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[234, 234]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 211, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[235, 235]], "note": "label heading"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[236, 240]], "assertion": "preregistered replication, individual-level referee bias measures, match-level analysis, mediation analysis, and experimental/quasi-experimental designs are recommended as next steps but have not been carried out", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["future research"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 213, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[241, 241]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 214, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[242, 242]], "note": "label heading"}, {"id": 215, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[243, 246]], "note": "conditional speculation about real-world implications if replicated"}, {"id": 216, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[247, 247]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 217, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[248, 248]], "note": "horizontal rule"}, {"id": 218, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[249, 249]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 219, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[250, 250]], "note": "section heading"}, {"id": 220, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[251, 251]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 221, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[252, 257]], "assertion": "the analysis code (final_analysis.py) fully documents data loading/exclusions, variable construction, model specifications, bootstrap procedure (seed 42), and sensitivity analyses, and is fully reproducible", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility", "final_analysis.py"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 222, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[258, 258]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 223, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[259, 259]], "note": "label heading"}, {"id": 224, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[260, 260]], "note": "code fence"}, {"id": 225, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[261, 261]], "assertion": "the analysis is reproduced by running `python final_analysis.py`", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproduction command"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 226, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[262, 262]], "note": "code fence"}, {"id": 227, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[263, 263]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 228, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[264, 264]], "assertion": "all results, including bootstrap random number generation, are seeded for exact reproducibility", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["random seed", "reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 229, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[265, 265]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 230, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[266, 266]], "note": "horizontal rule"}, {"id": 231, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[267, 267]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 232, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[268, 268]], "note": "section heading"}, {"id": 233, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[269, 269]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 234, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[270, 270]], "assertion": "the raw dataset comprises 146,028 dyads from 2,053 players and 3,147 referees across four leagues (2012-13), rated by two blind independent raters, with an analytical sample of 124,621 after excluding missing skin tone", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dataset provenance", "sample composition"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 235, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[271, 271]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 236, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[272, 272]], "note": "code availability statement"}, {"id": 237, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[273, 273]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 238, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[274, 274]], "note": "horizontal rule"}, {"id": 239, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[275, 275]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 240, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[276, 276]], "note": "appendix heading"}, {"id": 241, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[277, 277]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 242, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[278, 278]], "assertion": "dichotomization cutpoints were systematically evaluated by fitting bivariate models (darkSkin + log_games) per threshold and comparing z-statistics for the darkSkin coefficient", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["specification search", "cutpoints"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 243, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[279, 279]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 244, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[280, 280]], "note": "table header"}, {"id": 245, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[281, 281]], "note": "table separator"}, {"id": 246, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[282, 282]], "assertion": "at cutpoint >0.0625: N dark 90,898, N light 33,723, rates 1.31% vs 1.11%, diff 0.20pp, z=2.78, p=0.005", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["cutpoint search table"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 247, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[283, 283]], "assertion": "at cutpoint >0.125 (primary): N dark 73,022, N light 51,599, rates 1.37% vs 1.10%, diff 0.26pp, z=4.13, p<0.001", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["cutpoint search table", "primary specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 248, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[284, 284]], "assertion": "at cutpoint >0.25: N dark 34,505, N light 90,116, rates 1.36% vs 1.22%, diff 0.14pp, z=2.03, p=0.042", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["cutpoint search table"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 249, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[285, 285]], "assertion": "at cutpoint >0.375: N dark 28,896, N light 95,725, rates 1.34% vs 1.23%, diff 0.11pp, z=1.51, p=0.130", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["cutpoint search table"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 250, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[286, 286]], "assertion": "at cutpoint >0.5: N dark 19,907, N light 104,714, rates 1.32% vs 1.24%, diff 0.08pp, z=0.90, p=0.367", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["cutpoint search table"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 251, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[287, 287]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 252, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[288, 288]], "assertion": "the >0.125 cutpoint yielded the strongest effect (z=4.13) and was selected as the primary specification, described as the optimal choice for maximizing in-sample evidence", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cutpoint selection"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 253, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[289, 289]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 254, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[290, 290]], "note": "horizontal rule"}, {"id": 255, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[291, 291]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 256, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[292, 293]], "note": "report metadata: date and analyst"}, {"id": 257, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[294, 294]], "assertion": "the study design is self-labeled as exploratory, in-sample, hypothesis-advocacy analysis", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["study design"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 258, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[295, 295]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 259, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[296, 296]], "note": "tool-output closing tag"}]}}